	(lib_symbols)
	(text_box "Target specifications (Rev A, all boards on the 48 V bus; rationale in the Obsidian requirements page):\n- Input voltage: 48 V nominal (13S LiPo, 42–54.6 V), operating 36–60 V; all bus parts rated ≥ 100 V; HW overvoltage trip 65 V\n- Continuous phase current: 25 A (RO100 Lite rated 20 A + 25 %), with heatsink + fan at ≤ 50 °C ambient\n- Peak phase current: 65 A for 3 s (RO100 Lite peak 62 A); HW overcurrent trip 80 A; current sense range ±80 A\n- Switching frequency: 40 kHz default, 20–60 kHz configurable; current loop at PWM rate\n- Max electrical frequency: ≥ 2 kHz (RO80 KV105 no-load: 5040 rpm × 21 pole pairs = 1.76 kHz)\n- Supported motors: 24–48 V rated, 2.85–20 A cont., 14–21 pole pairs, 0.12–1.7 Ω, 103–580 µH line (RO40 / RO80 / RO100)\n- Position feedback: sensored drive; 3× Hall input required (commutation), plus encoder input for FOC/position and motor NTC input\n- Fieldbus: EtherCAT, 2 ports (IN/OUT), 1 kHz cycle baseline (4 kHz capable), Distributed Clocks\n- Logic rails: 5 V ≤ 400 mA, 3.3 V ≤ 600 mA, regulators ≤ 70 % load; ambient −20…50 °C"
